<!--
  Auto Backup / full-backup exclusions for API 23-30 (`android:fullBackupContent`).

  `android:allowBackup="false"` already excludes the whole app from cloud backup
  and device transfer. These rules are the second layer required by
  docs/design/security-checklist-2026-10-31.md S5 and by plan R11's
  `noBackupFilesDir` semantics: if a later change ever turns backup on, the
  sensitive paths below must stay off the wire without anyone having to
  rediscover them.

  The paths are the real ones read from the code, not guesses:
    * databases/phonedsh-domain.db*  <- SqliteConnectionFactory.DEFAULT_DATABASE_NAME
                                       ("phonedsh-domain.db") via context.getDatabasePath
    * files/xl                       <- ProbeEngineViewModel.WORKSPACE_DIRECTORY ("xl");
                                       WAL segments + workspace files
    * files/worker, worker.version   <- WorkerAssets.BUNDLE_DIR / VERSION_FILE
                                       (the materialized copy of the APK asset)
    * no_backup/secure-store         <- AndroidSecureStore STORE_DIR under
                                       Context.noBackupFilesDir (dataDir/no_backup)

  The backup XML format has no globs, so the SQLite side files are listed
  explicitly; `-journal` is included for completeness (the app uses WAL mode,
  but a rollback-journal moment must not open a hole either).
-->
<full-backup-content>
    <exclude domain="database" path="phonedsh-domain.db" />
    <exclude domain="database" path="phonedsh-domain.db-wal" />
    <exclude domain="database" path="phonedsh-domain.db-shm" />
    <exclude domain="database" path="phonedsh-domain.db-journal" />

    <exclude domain="file" path="xl" />
    <exclude domain="file" path="worker" />
    <exclude domain="file" path="worker.version" />

    <!-- noBackupFilesDir is skipped by the platform itself; naming it keeps the
         rule honest if the store ever moves. The Keystore-wrapped key material
         never leaves AndroidKeyStore, and this covers the software-key fallback. -->
    <exclude domain="root" path="no_backup/secure-store" />
</full-backup-content>
